=== <code>{{SlayerTier|1}}</code> ===

The '''Riftstalker Bloodfiend''' constantly drains {{stat|hearts|0.5}} every second. Every few seconds{{infoneeded}}, or if the player is too far away, it will enter its Spectral Form to move. It will return back to normal once it lands. Once the boss is at half health, it will use its Mania ability, becoming immune for 26 seconds. A circle of red blocks will spawn, along with a green ring inside of it. The player must stand in the green ring to not get their {{stat|hearts|2}} taken. Being outside of the 13 blocks circle incurs {{stat|hearts|3}} every second. As a vampire, when at or below {{stat|hp|125}}, it takes {{stat|rift damage|+1000}} when attacked by a player with a [[Steak Stake]].

=== <code>{{SlayerTier|2}}</code> ===

Instead of draining {{stat|hearts|0.5}} every second and taking away {{stat|hearts|2}} per failed Mania, the boss now drains {{stat|hearts|1}} every second and takes away {{stat|hearts|3}} per failed Mania. Now, the Mania phase starts upon the boss reaching 60% health. Every 7 seconds, a pair of Twinclaws spawn, with one in front of the boss and one behind the boss. The frontal claw is shot towards one of the players fighting the boss, and takes away {{stat|hearts|3}} upon hitting any players fighting the boss. The boss also spawns Clotgoyles that reduce the player's maximum {{stat|hearts}} by 1 after their Mania ability. After the Clotgoyles are killed, the hearts are returned to the player. They will respawn unless hit by the '''Riftstalker Bloodfiend'''{{'}}s Stonewrath. As a vampire, when at or below {{stat|hp|220}}, it takes {{stat|rift damage|+1000}} when attacked by a player with a [[Steak Stake]].

=== <code>{{SlayerTier|3}}</code> ===

Instead of taking away {{stat|hearts|3}} per Twinclaws attack and {{stat|hearts|3}} per failed Mania, the boss now takes away {{stat|hearts|5}} per Twinclaws attack and {{stat|hearts|5}} per failed Mania. The boss has 2 Mania attacks now, starting at {{stat|hp|75%}} and {{stat|hp|40%}}. During Mania attacks, the boss uses its Impel ability, during which players have to complete the boss's order (one of the following: '''CLICK UP''', '''CLICK DOWN''', '''JUMP''', '''SNEAK''') within 2.5s, or else {{stat|hearts|5}} are taken away. After the first Mania attack, the boss starts the Stonewrath ability. After the second Mania attack, the boss launches a spring made of candles to a nearby location. It can be compacted by clicking on it while alternating left and right click. The spring must be fully compacted within 15s or everything explodes and all players fighting it die. As a vampire, when at or below {{stat|hp|360}}, it takes {{stat|rift damage|+1000}} when attacked by a player with a [[Steak Stake]].

=== <code>{{SlayerTier|4}}</code> ===

Instead of taking away {{stat|hearts|5}} per Twinclaws attack, {{stat|hearts|5}} per failed Mania and {{stat|hearts|3}} when out of the Mania circle, the boss now takes away {{stat|hearts|6}} hearts for each of these attacks. Additionally, impels now have to be completed within 2s. The Twinclaws attack can now be used during the Mania attacks. As a vampire, when at or below {{stat|hp|480}}, it takes {{stat|rift damage|+1000}} when attacked by a player with a [[Steak Stake]].

=== <code>{{SlayerTier|5}}</code> ===

Instead of taking away {{stat|hearts|6}} per Twinclaws attack, {{stat|hearts|6}} per failed Mania, {{stat|hearts|5}} per failed Impel and draining {{stat|hearts|1}} per second, the boss now takes away {{stat|hearts|8}} per Twinclaws attack, {{stat|hearts|15}} per failed Mania, {{stat|hearts|20}} per failed Impel and drains {{stat|hearts|1.5}} per second. The boss has a new Blood Ichor attack, which frequently spawns an ichor nearby which must be destroyed within 25s. When Twinclaws are thrown towards the Blood Ichor, it breaks. As a vampire, when at or below {{stat|hp|600}}, it takes {{stat|rift damage|+1000}} when attacked by a player with a [[Steak Stake]].

== Tips ==
*Due to {{Item|Unfanged Vampire Part}} being relatively common, and gear for this slayer not being particularly expensive or difficult to obtain, regardless of player's progress outside of the Rift Dimension, fighting {{SlayerTier|4}} or {{SlayerTier|5}} of '''Riftstalker Bloodfiend''' can be quite a good way to grind {{c}}.

== Bugs ==
*The sounds from the {{AN|Killer Spring}} ability on Tier 3 and above may overload Minecraft's sound engine, resulting in all game sounds being completely muted for a few seconds.
**This can be alleviated by muting the {{code|entity.wither.spawn}} sound using a mod (such as [[mod:sound-controller|Sound Controller]]) or a resource pack. The mod [[mod:skyhanni|SkyHanni]] also provides an option to mute excess sounds without muting wither sounds entirely.
*During Stonewrath, the <code>{{SlayerTier|5}}</code> '''Riftstalker Bloodfiend''' is able to spawn Blood Ichors, resulting in Blood Ichors spawning in inaccesible spots.
**This can be partially mitigated by making sure to spawn the boss somewhere the boss won't be able to spawn an ichor during Stonewrath.
**Or phase the boss into Mania before it casts Stonewrath to completely avoid this bug

== Trivia ==
*Although the ability description for Mania says it lasts {{Green|22s}}, it actually lasts {{Green|26s}}.
*Damage from Coagulation happens every 1.5 seconds. This causes each tick to deal {{red|0.75/1.5/1.5/1.5/2.25}}{{stat|hearts|icononly=true}}, and for {{SlayerTier|5}} with an active Blood Ichor, it becomes {{red|3}}{{stat|hearts|icononly=true}} per tick.
*The {{Motes}} earned from spawning and killing the '''Riftstalker Bloodfiend''' can pay off the cost of starting the Slayer Quest.
**As such, this slayer has potential to guarantee profit both inside the Rift Dimension and out. The {{Item|Vampiric Melon}}s and {{Item|Splatter Crux}}es dropped by spawning mobs can be sold for {{Motes}} in addition to most boss drops. The rest can be sold outside the Rift Dimension for {{c}}.
*The ability {{aqua|Impel}} is derived from modern vampire media in which vampires are sometimes depicted as beings capable of hypnotizing their victims with a single glance.<ref>https://vampires.fandom.com/wiki/Hypnosis#Vampires_and_Hypnosis</ref>
**Hypnosis is not found in traditional vampire folklore, but instead first appeared in works of 19th-century writers such as Bram Stoker, who popularized the idea of vampires using mesmerizing gazes to entrance their victims. In modern vampire media vampires are occasionally shown to mind control their victims, forcing them to do their bidding.<ref>https://vampires.fandom.com/wiki/Hypnosis</ref>
*Despite the {{Skl|Combat}} skill or its leveling rewards not having any impact in the Rift, the {{SlayerTier|5}} '''Riftstalker Bloodfiend''' requires {{Skill|Combat|25}} to summon.

